title:string = "AEON Processing Walkthrough"
description:string = "Follow one AEON document through source text, canonical form, assignment events, schema validation, meaning validation, and Tonic materialization."
activePage:string = "walkthrough-processing"
keywords:list<string> = ["processing", "pipeline", "canonical", "AES", "AEOS", "schema validation", "materialization", "tonic"]

page:node = <page(
  <section @{type:string = "feature", level:string = "1"} (
    <kicker("Processing Walkthrough")>
    <title("Watch one AEON document move from edited text to accepted runtime form.")>
    <heading("Show the pipeline, one boundary at a time.")>
    <copy("The language walkthroughs introduce the surface syntax. This page follows a small document through the processing stages that make AEON useful in real systems: source text, [& canonical form|Canonical form], assignment events, schema validation, meaning validation, and [& Tonic] materialization.")>
    <copy("The examples borrow the shape of the Hello World, Goodnight Moon, and Sayonara Sun demos: friendly messages, explicit datatypes, staged validation, and a runtime object that only appears after the consumer has accepted the document.")>
    <actions(
      <action @{href:string = "#edited-source", primary:boolean = true} ("Start with source")>
      <action @{href:string = "/playground.php"} ("Open playground")>
    )>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature", id:string = "edited-source"} (
    <kicker("Step 1")>
    <title("Start with the document the user edits.")>
    <copy("The edited document is ordinary AEON. It declares strict mode, then gives the consumer a greeting configuration with a custom datatype label, a separator version, two messages, and the small numeric window used by the app.")>
    <code(`
aeon:header = {
  mode:string = "strict"
}

moon:greeting = {
  version:ver[.] = ^1.0.0
  daytime:string = "Hello World"
  nighttime:string = "Goodbye Moon"
  hoursBeforeMidnight:number = 4
  hoursAfterMidnight:number = 5
}
`)>
    <annotations(
      <annotation(
        <label("Visible claims")>
        <copy("The document says it wants strict mode and that moon is a greeting. It does not prove those claims by itself.")>
      )>
      <annotation(
        <label("Typed values")>
        <copy("The messages, version, and hour fields keep their intended value families visible before any runtime object exists.")>
      )>
    )>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 2")>
    <title("Canonical view reproduces the same document in a stable form.")>
    <copy("Canonical form is not a new meaning layer. It is the same document normalized for stable comparison, signing, hashing, cache keys, review diffs, and reproducible processing.")>
    <code(`
aeon:header = {
  mode:string = "strict"
}
moon:greeting = {
  daytime:string = "Hello World"
  hoursAfterMidnight:number = 5
  hoursBeforeMidnight:number = 4
  nighttime:string = "Goodbye Moon"
  version:ver[.] = ^1.0.0
}
`)>
    <copy("The consumer can compare this stable representation without pretending that canonicalization has performed domain validation. It has only made the representation deterministic.")>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 3")>
    <title("Parsing produces assignment events before application objects.")>
    <copy("AEON does not need to jump directly from text into a runtime model. The parser can expose a stream of assignments: each event has a path, value family, datatype claim, and source order.")>
    <code(`
event:object = {
  order:number = 1
  path:string = "$.moon"
  nodeType:string = "ObjectNode"
  datatype:string = "greeting"
}

event:object = {
  order:number = 4
  path:string = "$.moon.nighttime"
  nodeType:string = "StringLiteral"
  value:string = "Goodbye Moon"
}

event:object = {
  order:number = 5
  path:string = "$.moon.hoursBeforeMidnight"
  nodeType:string = "IntegerLiteral"
  value:number = 4
}
`)>
    <copy("This is the point where tooling can inspect what was written without accepting the document as valid config yet.")>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 4")>
    <title("The consumer applies a schema to the stream.")>
    <copy("A [& schema|Schema] checks that the required paths exist and that each path carries the expected literal family. The schema does not coerce values, repair types, or silently decide that a different shape is close enough.")>
    <code(`
aeos:schema = {
  id:string = "example.greeting.v1"
  version:string = "1"
  rules:list<object> = [
    {
      path:sansa = $.moon
      constraints:object = {
        required:boolean = true
        type:string = "ObjectNode"
        datatype:string = "greeting"
      }
    }
    {
      path:sansa = $.moon.version
      constraints:object = {
        required:boolean = true
        type:string = "SeparatorLiteral"
      }
    }
    {
      path:sansa = $.moon.daytime
      constraints:object = {
        required:boolean = true
        type:string = "StringLiteral"
      }
    }
    {
      path:sansa = $.moon.nighttime
      constraints:object = {
        required:boolean = true
        type:string = "StringLiteral"
      }
    }
    {
      path:sansa = $.moon.hoursBeforeMidnight
      constraints:object = {
        required:boolean = true
        type:string = "IntegerLiteral"
      }
    }
  ]
}
`)>
    <code(`
schemaResult:validation = {
  status:toggle = on
  accepted:list<string> = [
    "$.moon"
    "$.moon.version"
    "$.moon.daytime"
    "$.moon.nighttime"
    "$.moon.hoursBeforeMidnight"
    "$.moon.hoursAfterMidnight"
  ]
}
`)>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 5")>
    <title("Meaning validation checks the business rules the schema should not guess.")>
    <copy("The schema can prove the shape. It cannot decide whether the greeting window makes sense for this application. That belongs to [& consumer|Consumer] policy, profile rules, or domain validators.")>
    <code(`
meaningRules:object = {
  datatype:string = "greeting"
  hoursBeforeMidnight:range = ^0..6
  hoursAfterMidnight:range = ^0..6
  daytime:required = yes
  nighttime:required = yes
}

meaningResult:validation = {
  status:toggle = on
  checks:list<string> = [
    "moon datatype is greeting"
    "hoursBeforeMidnight is between 0 and 6"
    "hoursAfterMidnight is between 0 and 6"
    "daytime and nighttime messages are present"
  ]
}
`)>
    <copy("A consumer can make those rules stricter in one context and looser in another without changing what AEON Core is responsible for.")>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 6")>
    <title("Only then does a Tonic materialize the runtime object.")>
    <copy("A Tonic is where the accepted document becomes something useful to an application. In the Moon example it can become a Greeting object. In the Sun example the same staged pattern becomes a Farewell object.")>
    <code(`
tonic:materialized = {
  class:string = "Greeting"
  sourcePath:string = "$.moon"
  daytime:string = "Hello World"
  nighttime:string = "Goodbye Moon"
  activeWindow:string = "19:00-05:00"
  messageAt22:string = "Goodbye Moon"
}
`)>
    <copy("The runtime object is accepted for this context because the consumer walked through the boundaries it cares about: compile errors, datatype checks, schema rules, meaning rules, and finalization errors. Those checks do not prove external truth; they establish that the consumer chose to materialize this claim under its policy.")>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "feature"} (
    <kicker("Step 7")>
    <title("The same shape scales to the Sayonara Sun example.")>
    <copy("Once the pattern is routine, the repetitive checks can move into helper functions while the config loader still reads in phase order: load, require datatype, require schema, require ranges, require clean finalization, then construct the Tonic.")>
    <code(`
sun:farewell = {
  version:ver[.] = ^1.1.0
  daytime:string = "Hello, Sun"
  farewell:string = "Sayonara, Sun"
  sunsetHour:number = 18
  cooldownHours:number = 3
}

loader:sequence = [
  "loadAeonDocument"
  "requireDatatype"
  "requireSchema"
  "requireUnsignedIntegerRange"
  "requireNoFinalizeErrors"
  "new Farewell"
]
`)>
    <copy("The code becomes shorter, but the trust boundary stays visible. The helper layer reduces boilerplate without collapsing the phases.")>
  )>

  <section @{type:string = "cards"} (
    <kicker("Next")>
    <title("Continue into the side-channel model.")>
    <cards(
      <card(
        <topline("Annotation Walkthrough")>
        <heading("See annotations drive rendering")>
        <copy("Trace AEON data and node templates into an annotation stream, then into generated HTML.")>
        <href("/walkthrough-annotations.php")>
        <cta("Open annotation walkthrough")>
      )>
      <card(
        <topline("Templating Demo")>
        <heading("Try the app-like renderer")>
        <copy("Edit data and template AEON side by side, then render the output in the browser.")>
        <href("/templating.php")>
        <cta("Open templating")>
      )>
      <card(
        <topline("Playground")>
        <heading("Test strict parsing yourself")>
        <copy("Use the playground to try source documents, invalid forms, and stream output.")>
        <href("/playground.php")>
        <cta("Open playground")>
      )>
    )>
  )>
)>
